      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s post office opened in 1904, and that same year Protestant and Catholic churches were built, one doubling as a school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newmexicoghosttowns.net/encino-nm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A mercantile built in 1905 doubled as the depot and remained the only store until 1908, when a lumber company opened.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newmexicoghosttowns.net/encino-nm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Encino’s gym, now housing city offices, is considered picturesque and has been eyed as a potential film industry location.",
